WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:03.234
(bongo music)

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:04.363
- OK.

00:00:04.363 --> 00:00:05.213
Action.

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:06.444
(suspenseful music)

00:00:06.444 --> 00:00:09.054
(yelling and fighting)

00:00:09.054 --> 00:00:11.617
In Wakaliwood we do action,

00:00:11.617 --> 00:00:12.736
we do horror,

00:00:12.736 --> 00:00:15.007
and we do African witchcraft.

00:00:15.007 --> 00:00:15.949
(yells in foreign language)

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.761
We're always improvising here.

00:00:17.761 --> 00:00:19.502
Whatever we feel like we want,

00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:20.335
we do it.

00:00:20.335 --> 00:00:21.168
(gunfire)

00:00:21.168 --> 00:00:24.168
(suspenseful music)

00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:28.159
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.784
- [Narrator] Wakaliga,

00:00:40.784 --> 00:00:43.216
a slum in Uganda's capital of Kampala,

00:00:43.216 --> 00:00:45.152
is home to a burgeoning, low-budget

00:00:45.152 --> 00:00:47.657
DIY cinema industry called,

00:00:47.657 --> 00:00:48.574
Wakaliwood.

00:00:50.057 --> 00:00:52.905
Think action-packed
comedies with shootouts,

00:00:52.905 --> 00:00:53.976
car chases,

00:00:53.976 --> 00:00:55.361
explosions,

00:00:55.361 --> 00:00:56.961
zombies.

00:00:56.961 --> 00:00:59.024
All with a shoestring budget.

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:01.304
- Wakaliwood is a name that comes from

00:01:01.304 --> 00:01:02.578
the word Wakaliga,

00:01:02.578 --> 00:01:05.074
where I grew up and where I am right now

00:01:05.074 --> 00:01:06.057
and wood,

00:01:06.057 --> 00:01:07.864
from the Hollywood because all movies

00:01:07.864 --> 00:01:09.377
we knew were from Hollywood.

00:01:09.377 --> 00:01:10.354
All set?

00:01:10.354 --> 00:01:11.187
- [Actors] Yes!

00:01:11.187 --> 00:01:12.020
- OK.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:12.853
Action.

00:01:12.853 --> 00:01:15.378
My name is Isaac Nabwana Godfrey Geoffrey,

00:01:15.378 --> 00:01:19.167
the founder of Wakaliwood
and the director here.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.178
I do editing;

00:01:20.178 --> 00:01:21.960
I do camera shootings.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:22.793
Action.

00:01:22.793 --> 00:01:24.960
And I write action movies.

00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:31.617
I started making movies in 2005,

00:01:31.617 --> 00:01:34.680
but the dream was back way in 1986.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:35.513
Around that,

00:01:35.513 --> 00:01:36.991
when I was a teenager.

00:01:36.991 --> 00:01:39.681
- [Narrator] To date, Isaac
has made over 40 movies,

00:01:39.681 --> 00:01:42.839
most for nothing more that $200.

00:01:42.839 --> 00:01:44.769
He is Wakaliwood's only director for now,

00:01:44.769 --> 00:01:46.456
but people from all over have come

00:01:46.456 --> 00:01:50.319
to support Wakaliwood
in all kinds of ways.

00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:52.809
- My name was Alan Hofmanis.

00:01:52.809 --> 00:01:54.638
My name now in Uganda,

00:01:54.638 --> 00:01:57.817
is Alan Ssali Owe Nkima Musajja Wakabaka

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.067
Ne Mafene Yesu Muganda Laptop Hofmanis.

00:02:05.785 --> 00:02:08.480
So if you enjoy muzungu getting beaten,

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.010
wait til you see muzungu getting eaten.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:11.843
(laughs)

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:12.898
- [Narrator] His actors aren't paid,

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:15.106
and most have side jobs
ranging from teachers,

00:02:15.106 --> 00:02:16.968
nurses and lawyers.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:17.992
- I train my own.

00:02:17.992 --> 00:02:20.409
I believe that everyone can be a star.

00:02:20.409 --> 00:02:22.264
I get them from all over the country.

00:02:22.264 --> 00:02:27.181
We welcome everyone because we
feel like movies are family.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.663
The props department is like a workshop

00:02:32.663 --> 00:02:35.999
where we make everything we
want which we cannot buy.

00:02:35.999 --> 00:02:37.440
We can do our own lights;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.158
we can do our own gib;

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.863
we can do our own dollies,

00:02:40.863 --> 00:02:42.291
and everything.

00:02:42.291 --> 00:02:43.440
The guns.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:47.039
There's so many things we
needed, and we cannot buy.

00:02:47.039 --> 00:02:48.111
By improvising,

00:02:48.111 --> 00:02:50.382
we make them in his workshop there.

00:02:50.382 --> 00:02:51.349
(cocks gun)

00:02:51.349 --> 00:02:54.766
I'm very good at, you know,
using the little I have.

00:02:58.390 --> 00:02:59.431
- [Narrator] His first film,

00:02:59.431 --> 00:03:00.679
Who Killed Captain Alex?,

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:04.353
brought widespread
attention to Wakaliwood.

00:03:04.353 --> 00:03:05.729
After uploading it to YouTube,

00:03:05.729 --> 00:03:10.570
it quickly went viral and gained
a cult following worldwide.

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:13.778
- I knew no one had ever done
an action movie in Africa,

00:03:13.778 --> 00:03:15.489
so I knew if it goes out,

00:03:15.489 --> 00:03:18.474
people will at least give
it, you know, a chance.

00:03:18.474 --> 00:03:21.682
Everyone loved it and
Captain Alex became a hit.

00:03:21.682 --> 00:03:23.137
- [Narrator] What started as a dream

00:03:23.137 --> 00:03:24.722
that was borderline fantasy,

00:03:24.722 --> 00:03:27.313
has turned into a
full-fledged production house

00:03:27.313 --> 00:03:29.324
that has gone mainstream.

00:03:29.324 --> 00:03:30.931
(yells)

00:03:30.931 --> 00:03:33.195
- I did not go to school to learn movies.

00:03:33.195 --> 00:03:34.530
I don't know festivals;

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.218
I don't know awards.

00:03:36.218 --> 00:03:40.220
When I make movies my main goal
is for the people to enjoy.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.780
When they watch them they will
laugh because it is funny.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.035
It was comedy to us, everything.

00:03:45.035 --> 00:03:47.233
So I feel like life
without, you know, laughing,

00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:49.900
laughing without comedy is not life.

